{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1524912-splats-as-ancient-gods","id":1524912,"title":"Splats as Ancient Gods","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-02T06:57:13-07:00","id":1524912,"title":"Splats as Ancient Gods","content":"I was reading Persephone Rising and the thought of ancient and powerful members of the splats being regarded as Gods in the ancient world was interesting. What gods do you think fit the various splats? Was Osiris a Promethean? Was Pan one of the Lost? Was the Morrigan one of the bound? <br /> <br /> Perhaps equally important, do you think any of the non-immortal ancient gods could still be around today? Weird things happen at very high power stat levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T07:10:49-07:00","id":1524913,"title":"","content":"So, Dark Ages (can't remember if it's 1 or 2) confirms that at least some of the Greek Gods were True Fae, or at the very least there were True Fae masquerading as the Greek Gods. Although not stated anywhere, though I could be misremembering, I do think Osiris as the founder of the Osiran Lineage makes total sense, after all we do have Adam Frankenstein for the Frankensteins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T07:22:41-07:00","id":1524914,"title":"","content":"Some of the \u2018demons\u2019 ie. foreign gods described in the Bible could have been Deathless. Mammon, Moloch, Baal, Abaddon, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T10:16:47-07:00","id":1524929,"title":"","content":"It is really up to what you the game you are playing and the story you want to tell. Pretty much every game has <i>something</i> that can either be a diety or masquerade as one. I intentionally wrote the Colossi into Requiem for Rome 2e to serve that niche and I ever get Night Horrors: Kindly Ones up on the Vault, I'm planning to have an example of a True Fae who claims to be Posidon with his epithets as his Titles.<br /> <br /> I also have a nebulous idea for a Vault product that talks about the Astral manifestations of the divine, since those all exist in the Temenos as well. I'm very much of the opinions that those Goetia are very powerful, very active, and the question of &quot;are they the genuine article&quot; is largely irrelevant. That is a mortal way of thinking about things, the divine are transcendent.<br /> <br /> No ETA on either of them, they are just ideas right now, but that may give a starting place for people to think about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 11-02-2023, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T15:08:50-07:00","id":1524937,"title":"","content":"Morrigan may have been a vampire, high blood potency, either still alive and going by Morrigan or in torpor, or has ascended somehow how being the vampiric state (possibly using cruac) to become an aspect of the Crone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T15:42:31-07:00","id":1524938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1524912-splats-as-ancient-gods?p=1524937#post1524937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Morrigan may have been a vampire, high blood potency, either still alive and going by Morrigan or in torpor, or has ascended somehow how being the vampiric state (possibly using cruac) to become an aspect of the Crone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit kindred fit much better for The Morrigan than the bound, but as I was inspired by Persephone as a vampire I wanted to use non kindred examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T16:18:36-07:00","id":1524940,"title":"","content":"In a Requiem chronicle i did mess with the idea of Red Jack &amp; Blood Mary being guises of Tezcatlipoca &amp; Tlazoteotl respectively, but don't remember if i went much farther than that when it comes to divine, though i would bring mythologic and folkloric touches into the table all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T14:14:24-08:00","id":1525539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1524912-splats-as-ancient-gods?p=1524940#post1524940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a Requiem chronicle i did mess with the idea of Red Jack &amp; Blood Mary being guises of Tezcatlipoca &amp; Tlazoteotl respectively, but don't remember if i went much farther than that when it comes to divine, though i would bring mythologic and folkloric touches into the table all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I legit would <i>not</i> be surprised if at least <u>part</u> of the reason as to why the Aztecs had such a heavy focus on things blood and hearts in their religion was that of Vampires with particularly high BP being present, &amp; pretending (or genuinely believing) that they were certain members of the pantheon, or at least the Champions/Prophets/Avatars thereof.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T14:30:47-08:00","id":1525541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1524912-splats-as-ancient-gods?p=1525539#post1525539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, I legit would <i>not</i> be surprised if at least <u>part</u> of the reason as to why the Aztecs had such a heavy focus on things blood and hearts in their religion was that of Vampires with particularly high BP being present, &amp; pretending (or genuinely believing) that they were certain members of the pantheon, or at least the Champions/Prophets/Avatars thereof.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadows of Mexico offers some interesting ideas on the matter of relations between the kindred and pre-columbian deities, that can get only more engrossing and entertaining if one has access to Mythologies, Night Horrors: Wicked Dead, Geist: the Sin Eaters &amp; or Changeling: the Lost to mix, match &amp; tinker with. Plus, if memory tricks me not, there's a Dark Era revolving around Demon &amp; Forsakem in the Aztec Empire, to boot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T15:31:15-08:00","id":1525544,"title":"","content":"I believe that Dark ETA is Demon + Skin Thief (merit template).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T14:02:32-08:00","id":1525657,"title":"","content":"I second <i>Shadows of Mexico</i>. <br /> <br /> Considering the first vampire-books I read were Ann Rice, of course the Splats were ancient-gods; in my games, the Supers, had the role of priests in human-society and weren't necessarily outsiders. There's one that lives in a dark-cave and you can only converse with it at night. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1524912-splats-as-ancient-gods?p=1525539#post1525539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, I legit would <i>not</i> be surprised if at least <u>part</u> of the reason as to why the Aztecs had such a heavy focus on things blood and hearts in their religion was that of Vampires with particularly high BP being present, &amp; pretending (or genuinely believing) that they were certain members of the pantheon, or at least the Champions/Prophets/Avatars thereof.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I had a game from the Immortals-Book; a Blood Bather was behind the sacrifices. And there was another Mayan City-State with a Purified. <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T06:28:04-08:00","id":1525840,"title":"","content":"Also, in Dark Ages, there's the Followers of Set that are, based in the Baltic-Peninsula; now, how on Earth did ancient Egyptian religion get up there is a mystery (they were probably pushed there by other two-fangs). <br /> <br /> Also, I had a OWoD game in which the antagonists was an ancient Gangrel that lived in a lake called the Knack, by the Vikings (actually, it was the Dzaplonenya formally known as the Crunna), that dwelt in that lake for centuries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}